# The SDR build variant.
#
# The ESP-SDR browser viewer (https://espargos.net/espsdr/app/) and the
# native capture app need the whole of SRAM block 2 (0x40840000) as the
# capture bank, which takes 128 KB out of the heap. The image with the Zigbee
# and the Thread stacks still links below the bank (about 2 KB to spare), but
# at run time the Zigbee and the BLE apps are left with 4-5 KB of heap
# (measured on hardware, 2026-11-25). This variant keeps the two stacks out,
# which gives the heap about 50 KiB more below the bank.
#
# The MININO_ZIGBEE_STACK and MININO_OPENTHREAD_STACK options take the
# components of those stacks out of the build (see the filters in
# main/CMakeLists.txt). The menus follow the same gate, so the apps of the
# stacks that are not compiled in disappear from the menu as well.
#
# To have SDR and Zigbee/Thread on the same device, use the combined variant
# (sdkconfig.sdr-full, make build-sdr-full) instead.
#
# Build it with:
#   idf.py @profiles/sdr/profile build
#
# or, from the Makefile:
#   make build-sdr

# The capture bank is reserved and the image is capped below it.
CONFIG_SDR_ENABLE=y

# The Zigbee and the Thread stacks stay out to leave heap next to the bank.
# CONFIG_MININO_ZIGBEE_STACK is not set
# CONFIG_MININO_OPENTHREAD_STACK is not set
